  "posts": [
    {
      "slug": "why-the-oboro-light-line-is-exactly-3-px",
      "title": "Why the Oboro light line is exactly 3 px",
      "date": "2026-10-02",
      "categories": [
        "case-notes"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "identity",
        "motion"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/case1.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Every part of the Oboro identity is drawn from one line: the width of the lamp's own LED strip. Here is how a spec sheet became a brand.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The first thing Oboro sent us was not a mood board. It was a spec sheet for their smallest lamp, with one number circled in pencil: the LED strip, 3 mm wide. On screen at 1:1, that is three pixels.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">One line, every size</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We drew the logotype, the icons, the packaging rules and even the motion curves from that one line. When the line moves, it moves at the speed the lamp fades up: 400 milliseconds, eased out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If the brand is the light, the line should behave like the light.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Aya Morikawa, design director</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{theme}}/assets/images/case1.jpg\" alt=\"Matte grey boxes on black plinths crossed by a bright green line\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The packaging test: one grey card, one fluorescent line.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The rule turned out to be generous rather than strict. It told the team what not to do, and left everything else open.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "projecting-onto-board-marked-concrete",
      "title": "Projecting onto board-marked concrete",
      "date": "2026-09-24",
      "categories": [
        "case-notes"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "film",
        "interactive"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/case2.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Kosa Gallery has no flat walls. Our title sequence had to learn to love the board marks.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Concrete poured against timber boards keeps their grain forever. It is beautiful, and it is terrible for projection: every edge catches light and every hollow swallows it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tilt the plane, not the room</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After two nights of tests we stopped fighting the grain and tilted the projected plane eleven degrees, so the board lines run across it like scan lines. The wall became part of the film.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-dash\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-dash\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Projector: 10,000 lumens, ceiling mounted</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Loop: 18 minutes, cut to the opening hours</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Colour: one green, measured on the wall, not on the monitor</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The lesson we wrote on the studio wall afterwards: measure colour where people will see it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "a-swatch-book-you-can-watch",
      "title": "A swatch book you can watch",
      "date": "2026-09-15",
      "categories": [
        "process"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "packaging",
        "motion"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/case3.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Forty-eight papers, forty-eight eight-second films, one pair of hands. Notes from a week of filming paper.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Paper is hard to sell on a screen because the screen is the opposite of paper: flat, cold and lit from behind. So we filmed what designers actually do with a sample. They bend it, tear a corner and hold it to the light.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Same hands, same light, same eight seconds</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every film follows one script. The consistency is what makes the differences visible: you start to see which papers spring back and which ones fold quietly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>After forty-eight papers my hands knew the mill better than I did.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Nora Lind, designer</cite></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The films now sit beside every paper in the order form, and in the sample book there is a small window cut where the film would be.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "long-exposures-short-deadlines",
      "title": "Long exposures, short deadlines",
      "date": "2026-09-03",
      "categories": [
        "type-and-motion"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "film",
        "motion"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/case4.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Twenty idents in four weeks, each one drawn in a single thirty-second exposure. What we learned about planning for accidents.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A long exposure is honest: whatever the light did in those thirty seconds is the picture. You cannot fix it in the edit. That made the Hikari Night Walk idents the most nerve-racking and the most fun job of the year.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rehearse the hand, not the shot</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We practised every movement on paper first, then with a torch and a phone, then with the real camera. By the third night most idents took fewer than five tries.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-dash\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-dash\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Shoot at the darkest hour, not the latest one</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Wear black gloves; the camera sees everything</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Keep the failed takes: three of them became social films</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "the-long-table",
      "title": "The long table: how a week runs at Kiroku",
      "date": "2026-08-21",
      "categories": [
        "studio-life"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "behind-the-scenes"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/team.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Monday planning, Wednesday wobble, Friday tape. A week in the studio, hour by hour.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Nine people, one room, one long table. People ask how that works without everyone wearing headphones all day. The answer is a week with a shape.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Monday to Friday</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-index\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-index\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Monday:</strong> planning at ten, at the table, with coffee and no screens.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Tuesday and Wednesday:</strong> deep work. Wednesday is when things usually look worst; we have learned to expect it.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Thursday:</strong> cutting and fixing.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Friday:</strong> the tape. Every project shows its week to the client and to each other.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The tape is the most important habit we have. Nothing disappears into a three-month silence, and nobody gets a big reveal they did not ask for.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "variable-fonts-that-breathe",
      "title": "Variable fonts that breathe on screen",
      "date": "2026-08-07",
      "categories": [
        "type-and-motion"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "typography",
        "motion"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/hero.jpg",
      "excerpt": "Width and weight axes are the cheapest animation on the web. A few rules for using them without making people seasick.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A variable font holds a whole family in one file, and every axis is a slider you can animate. Our own website stretches its headline words along the width axis, and its footer wordmark widens when you point at it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Three rules</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"is-style-index\"} -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list is-style-index\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Animate one axis at a time.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Keep it slow: two seconds or more for anything that loops.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Stop everything when the visitor asks for reduced motion.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Used like this, type can feel alive without becoming a distraction. Used without rules, it is a screensaver.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    },
    {
      "slug": "one-camera-one-tripod",
      "title": "One camera, one tripod, one green line",
      "date": "2026-07-28",
      "categories": [
        "studio-life"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "tools",
        "behind-the-scenes"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/studio.jpg",
      "excerpt": "The kit behind most of our films fits in one bag. Here is what is in it, and why we keep it small.",
      "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Studios like ours can spend a fortune on kit. We decided early to keep ours small enough to carry up the stairs in one trip.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{theme}}/assets/images/studio.jpg\" alt=\"A camera on a tripod outlined in thin green light in a dark studio\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The whole camera department.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Small kit, more takes</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A small kit means we set up fast, and setting up fast means more takes. More takes beat better equipment nearly every time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
    }
  ],
